@startuml umd_device_lifecycle
' Device lifecycle: each transition is labelled with what triggers it.
' Explicit arrow directions keep the main flow top to bottom; the recovery loop (warm reset) points up so it does not reorder the ranks.
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

[*] -down-> Discovered : discover()
Discovered -down-> Constructed : TTDevice(model)
Constructed -down-> Initialized : init_tt_device()
Constructed -left-> Failed : firmware timeout / version mismatch
Initialized -down-> Operational : start_device()
Operational -right-> Faulted : exception (hang, SIGBUS, timeout)
Faulted -up-> Constructed : warm reset + re-open
Operational -down-> Closed : close_device() / destructor
Failed -down-> [*]
Closed -down-> [*]

Operational : read / write, firmware commands, DMA
@enduml
